      "updated": 1784436589551,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "APIs\n\n// fare estimation\nPOST /fare -> Fare\nBody: {\n  pickupLocation, \n  destination\n}\n\n\n// request ride\nPOST /rides -> Ride\nBody: {\n  fareId\n}\n\n\n// update driver endpoint\nPOST /drivers/location -> Success/Error\nBody: {\n        lat, long\n    }\n\n- Its called periodically by driver client\n\n\n// driver accept ride\nPATCH /rides/:rideId -> Ride\nBody: {\n  accept/deny\n}\n\nNote : userId in JWT, TS generated on server, fareEstimate object etc anything client generated should not be send in Body\nWe can't trust client, we just pass an Id, and retrieve that info from DB, the goal is not to leave our system in inconsistent state.\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "APIs\n\n// fare estimation\nPOST /fare -> Fare\nBody: {\n  pickupLocation, \n  destination\n}\n\n\n// request ride\nPOST /rides -> Ride\nBody: {\n  fareId\n}\n\n\n// update driver endpoint\nPOST /drivers/location -> Success/Error\nBody: {\n        lat, long\n    }\n\n- Its called periodically by driver client\n\n\n// driver accept ride\nPATCH /rides/:rideId -> Ride\nBody: {\n  accept/deny\n}\n\nNote : userId in JWT, TS generated on server, fareEstimate object etc anything client generated should not be send in Body\nWe can't trust client, we just pass an Id, and retrieve that info from DB, the goal is not to leave our system in inconsistent state.\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "Ab_TEEbyu9ebtjty1JerD",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -55328.308920679636,
      "y": -4720.105667266483,
      "width": 1567.45947265625,
      "height": 250,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a3",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 135044809,
      "version": 246,
      "versionNonce": 787073159,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1784438708095,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Notes\n\nDriver should be able to accept/decline request and navigate to pickup/dropff\n- After the Ride Matching Service determines the ranked list of eligible drivers, it sends a notification to the top driver on the list via APNs or FCM.\n- The driver receives a notification that a new ride request is available. They open the Driver Client app and accept the ride request, which sends a \n   PATCH request to our backend system with the rideID. a) If they decline the ride instead, the system will send a notification to the next driver on the list.\n- The API gateway receives the requests and routes it to the Ride Service.\n- The Ride Service receives the request and updates the status of the ride to \"accepted\" and updates the assigned driver accordingly. It then returns the \n   pickup location coordinates to the Driver Client.\n- With the coordinates in hand, the Driver uses on client GPS to navigate to the pickup location.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Notes\n\nDriver should be able to accept/decline request and navigate to pickup/dropff\n- After the Ride Matching Service determines the ranked list of eligible drivers, it sends a notification to the top driver on the list via APNs or FCM.\n- The driver receives a notification that a new ride request is available. They open the Driver Client app and accept the ride request, which sends a \n   PATCH request to our backend system with the rideID. a) If they decline the ride instead, the system will send a notification to the next driver on the list.\n- The API gateway receives the requests and routes it to the Ride Service.\n- The Ride Service receives the request and updates the status of the ride to \"accepted\" and updates the assigned driver accordingly. It then returns the \n   pickup location coordinates to the Driver Client.\n- With the coordinates in hand, the Driver uses on client GPS to navigate to the pickup location.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
